{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Mockable\/documentation\/Mockable\/Usage"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Mockable"}],"role":"article","title":"Usage","roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Larn how to use "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mockable"}]},{"type":"text","text":" to write readable and concise unit tests."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Given a protocol annotated with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Mockable"},{"type":"text","text":" macro:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Mockable","","@Mockable","protocol ProductService {","    var url: URL? { get set }","    func fetch(for id: UUID) async throws -> Product","    func checkout(with product: Product) throws","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A mock implementation named "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockProductService"},{"type":"text","text":" will be generated, that can be used in unit tests like this:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Mockable","","lazy var productService = MockProductService()","lazy var cartService = CartServiceImpl(productService: productService)","","func testCartService() async throws {","    let mockURL = URL(string: \"apple.com\")","    let mockError: ProductError = .notFound","    let mockProduct = Product(name: \"iPhone 15 Pro\")","","    given(productService)","        .fetch(for: .any).willReturn(mockProduct)","        .checkout(with: .any).willThrow(mockError)","","    try await cartService.checkout(with: mockProduct, using: mockURL)","","    verify(productService)","        .fetch(for: .value(mockProduct.id)).called(.atLeastOnce)","        .checkout(with: .value(mockProduct)).called(.once)","        .url(newValue: .value(mockURL)).setCalled(.once)","}"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Syntax","level":2,"anchor":"Syntax"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mockable"}]},{"type":"text","text":" has a declarative syntax that utilizes builders to construct "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"given"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"when"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verify"},{"type":"text","text":" clauses."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"When constructing any of these clauses, you always follow the same syntax:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clause type"},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"service"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"function builder"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"behavior builder"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In the following example where we use the previously introduced product service:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let id = UUID()","let error: ProductError = .notFound","","given(productService).fetch(for: .value(id)).willThrow(error)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"We specify the following:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"given"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": we want to register "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"return values"}],"type":"strong"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(productService)"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": we specify what mockable service we want to register return values for"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".fetch(for: .value(id))"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": we want to mock the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fetch(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method and constrain our behavior on calls with matching "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" parameters"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":".willThrow(error)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":": if "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fetch(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is called with the specified parameter value, we want an "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"error"}]},{"type":"text","text":" to be thrown"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Parameters","level":2,"anchor":"Parameters"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Function builders have "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"all parameters","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" from the original requirement but "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"encapsulate them","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" within the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/parameter","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" type."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"When constructing mockable clauses, you have to "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"specify parameter conditions","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" for every parameter of a function. There are three available options:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":".any","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Matches every call to the specified function, disregarding the actual parameter values."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":".value(Value)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Matches to calls with an identical value in the specified parameter."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":".matching((Value) -> Bool)","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Uses the provided closure to filter functions calls."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Computed properties have no parameters, but mutable properties get a ","type":"text"},{"code":"(newValue:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter in function builders that can be used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to constraint functionality on property assignment with a match condition. These ","type":"text"},{"code":"newValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conditions will only effect the ","type":"text"},{"code":"performOnGet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"performOnSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"getCalled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"setCalled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"clauses but will have no effect on return clauses.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are examples of using different parameter conditions:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ throw an error when `fetch(for:)` is called with `id`","given(productService).fetch(for: .value(id)).willThrow(error)","","\/\/ print \"Ouch!\" if product service is called with a product named \"iPhone 15 Pro\"","when(productService)","  .checkout(with: .matching { $0.name == \"iPhone 15 Pro\" })","  .perform { print(\"Ouch!\") }","","\/\/ assert if the fetch(for:) was called exactly once regardless of what id parameter it was called with","verify(productService).fetch(for: .any).called(.once)"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Given","level":2,"anchor":"Given"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Return values can be specified using a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"given(_ service:)"},{"type":"text","text":" clause. There are three return builders available:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/functionreturnbuilder\/willreturn(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Will store the given return value and use it to mock subsequent calls."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/throwingfunctionreturnbuilder\/willthrow(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Will store the given error and throw it in subsequent calls. Only available for throwing functions and properties."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/throwingfunctionreturnbuilder\/willproduce(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Will use the provided closure for mocking. The closure has the same signature as the mocked function, so for example a function that takes an integer returns a string and can throw will accept a closure of type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(Int) throws -> String"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/throwingfunctionreturnbuilder\/willhandle(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Registers a result type that automatically emits a value when successful or throws a failure."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The provided return values are used up in FIFO order and the last one is always kept for any further calls. Here are examples of using return clauses:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Throw an error for the first call and then return 'product' for every other call","given(productService)","    .fetch(for: .any).willThrow(error)","    .fetch(for: .any).willReturn(product)","","\/\/ Throw an error if the id parameter ends with a 0, return a product otherwise","given(productService)","    .fetch(for: .any).willProduce { id in","        if id.uuidString.last == \"0\" {","            throw error","        } else {","            return product","        }","    }"]},{"type":"heading","text":"When","level":2,"anchor":"When"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Side effects can be added using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"when(_ service:)"},{"type":"text","text":" clauses. There are three kind of side effects:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/functionactionbuilder\/perform(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Will register an operation to perform on invocations of the mocked function."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/propertyactionbuilder\/performonget(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Available for mutable properties only, will perform the provided operation on property access."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/propertyactionbuilder\/performonset(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Available for mutable properties only, will perform the provided operation on property assignment."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some examples of using side effects are:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ log calls to fetch(for:)","when(productService).fetch(for: .any).perform {","    print(\"fetch(for:) was called\")","}","","\/\/ log when url is accessed","when(productService).url().performOnGet {","    print(\"url accessed\")","}","","\/\/ log when url is set to nil","when(productService).url(newValue: .value(nil)).performOnSet {","    print(\"url set to nil\")","}"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Verify","level":2,"anchor":"Verify"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can verify invocations of your mock service using the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verify(_ service:)"},{"type":"text","text":" clause."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mockable"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" supports both ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"XCTest"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Testing"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" by using Pointfree’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/pointfreeco\/swift-issue-reporting"},{"text":" to dynamically report test failures with the appropriate test framework.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There are three kind of verifications:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/functionverifybuilder\/called(_:file:line:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Asserts invocation count based on the given value."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/propertyverifybuilder\/getcalled(_:file:line:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Available for mutable properties only, asserts property access count."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/propertyverifybuilder\/setcalled(_:file:line:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Available for mutable properties only, asserts property assignment count."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are some example assertions:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["verify(productService)","    \/\/ assert fetch(for:) was called between 1 and 5 times","    .fetch(for: .any).called(.from(1, to: 5))","    \/\/ assert checkout(with:) was called between exactly 10 times","    .checkout(with: .any).called(10)","    \/\/ assert url property was accessed at least 2 times","    .url().get(.moreOrEqual(to: 2))","    \/\/ assert url property was never set to nil","    .url(newValue: .value(nil)).setCalled(.never)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you are testing asynchronous code and cannot write sync assertions you can use the async counterparts of the above verifications:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/functionverifybuilder\/calledeventually(_:before:file:line:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Wait until timeout or invocation count satisfied."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/propertyverifybuilder\/getcalledeventually(_:before:file:line:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Wait until timeout or property access count satisfied."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/propertyverifybuilder\/setcalledeventually(_:before:file:line:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": Wait until timeout or property assignment count satisfied."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are some examples of async verifications:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["await verify(productService)","    \/\/ assert fetch(for:) was called between 1 and 5 times before default timeout (1 second)","    .fetch(for: .any).calledEventually(.from(1, to: 5))","    \/\/ assert checkout(with:) was called between exactly 10 times before 3 seconds","    .checkout(with: .any).calledEventually(10, before: .seconds(3))","    \/\/ assert url property was accessed at least 2 times before default timeout (1 second)","    .url().getCalledEventually(.moreOrEqual(to: 2))","    \/\/ assert url property was set to nil once","    .url(newValue: .value(nil)).setCalledEventually(.once)"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Relaxed Mode","level":2,"anchor":"Relaxed-Mode"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"By default, you must specify a return value for all requirements; otherwise, a fatal error will be thrown. The reason for this is to aid in the discovery (and thus the verification) of every called function when writing unit tests."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"However, it is common to prefer avoiding this strict default behavior in favor of a more relaxed setting, where,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for example, void or optional return values do not need explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"given"},{"type":"text","text":" registration."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the Use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/mockerpolicy","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (which is an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/swift\/optionset","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") to implicitly mock:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"only one kind of return value: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".relaxedMocked"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"construct a custom set of policies: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[.relaxedVoid, .relaxedOptional]"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"or opt for a fully relaxed mode: "},{"code":".relaxed","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You have two options to override the default strict behavior of the library:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"At "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"mock implementation level"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" you can override the mocker policy for each individual mock implementation in the initializer:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let relaxedMock = MockService(policy: [.relaxedOptional, .relaxedVoid])"]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"At "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"project level","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" you can set a custom default policy to use in every scenario by changing the default property of "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"MockerPolicy"}]},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["MockerPolicy.default = .relaxedVoid"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":".relaxedMocked","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" policy in combination with the "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/mocked","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" protocol can be used to set an implicit return value for custom (or even built in) types:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct Car {","    var name: String","    var seats: Int","}","","extension Car: Mocked {","    static var mock: Car {","        Car(name: \"Mock Car\", seats: 4)","    }","","    \/\/ Defaults to [mock] but we can ","    \/\/ provide a custom array of cars:","    static var mocks: [Car] {","        [","            Car(name: \"Mock Car 1\", seats: 4),","            Car(name: \"Mock Car 2\", seats: 4)","        ]","    }","}","","@Mockable","protocol CarService {","    func getCar() -> Car","    func getCars() -> [Car]","}","","func testCarService() {","    func test() {","        let mock = MockCarService(policy: .relaxedMocked)","        \/\/ Implictly mocked without a given registration:","        let car = mock.getCar()","        let cars = mock.getCars()","    }","}"]},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"⚠️ Relaxed mode will not work with generic return values as the type system is unable to locate the appropriate generic overload.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"},{"type":"heading","text":"Working with non-equatable Types","level":2,"anchor":"Working-with-non-equatable-Types"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Mockable","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" uses a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/matcher"},{"text":" internally to compare parameters.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"By default the matcher is able to compare any custom type that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (except when used in a generic function).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In special cases, when you","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"have non-equatable parameter types"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"need testing specific equality logic for a custom type"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"have generic functions that are used with custom concrete types"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"you can register your custom types with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Matcher.register()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" functions.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Here is how to do it:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ register an equatable type to the matcher because we use it in a generic function","Matcher.register(SomeEquatableType.self)","","\/\/ register a non-equatable type to the matcher","Matcher.register(Product.self, match: { $0.name == $1.name })","","\/\/ register a meta-type to the matcher","Matcher.register(HomeViewController.Type.self)","","\/\/ remove all previously registered custom types","Matcher.reset()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you see this error during tests:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["No comparator found for type XYZ. All non-equatable types must be ","registered using Matcher.register(_)."]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"remember to add the noted type to your ","type":"text"},{"code":"Matcher","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" using the ","type":"text"},{"code":"register()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" function.","type":"text"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Mockable\/documentation\/Mockable"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Mockable\/documentation\/Mockable\/Installation","doc:\/\/Mockable\/documentation\/Mockable\/Configuration"],"anchor":"Guides"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/mockable\/usage"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"kind":"article","references":{"https://kolos65.github.io/Mockable/documentation/mockable/propertyverifybuilder/setcalledeventually(_:before:file:line:)":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/propertyverifybuilder\/setcalledeventually(_:before:file:line:)","title":"setSalledEventually(_:before:)","url":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/propertyverifybuilder\/setcalledeventually(_:before:file:line:)","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setSalledEventually(_:before:)"}]},"https://kolos65.github.io/Mockable/documentation/mockable/throwingfunctionreturnbuilder/willhandle(_:)":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/throwingfunctionreturnbuilder\/willhandle(_:)","title":"willHandle(_ result:)","url":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/throwingfunctionreturnbuilder\/willhandle(_:)","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willHandle(_ result:)"}]},"https://kolos65.github.io/Mockable/documentation/mockable/mockerpolicy":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/mockerpolicy","title":"MockerPolicy","url":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/mockerpolicy","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockerPolicy"}]},"https://kolos65.github.io/Mockable/documentation/mockable/functionactionbuilder/perform(_:)":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/functionactionbuilder\/perform(_:)","title":"perform(_ action)","url":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/functionactionbuilder\/perform(_:)","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"perform(_ action)"}]},"https://kolos65.github.io/Mockable/documentation/mockable/propertyactionbuilder/performonset(_:)":{"type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/propertyactionbuilder\/performonset(_:)","title":"performOnSet(_ action:)","url":"https:\/\/kolos65.github.io\/Mockable\/documentation\/mockable\/propertyactionbuilder\/performonset